; Game status buffer entry at FE1C
@label=MAX1
g$FE1C DEFW $0000    ; Notebook name preserved. Current shipped read: first raw outer X-limit word
                     ; used by the hill/object suppression path. Visible major-entity passes seed
                     ; `FE1C/FE1E` from `XMAX/XMIN`; invisible cases park them at `$84D0/$84CF`.

; Game status buffer entry at FE1E
@label=MIN1
g$FE1E DEFW $0000    ; Companion raw outer X-limit word for `FE1C`.

; Game status buffer entry at FE20
@label=MAX2
g$FE20 DEFW $0000    ; Notebook name preserved. Current shipped read: second raw outer X-limit word
                     ; used by the hill/object suppression path, chiefly for the active obstacle /
                     ; object family selected at `0xA37B`.

; Game status buffer entry at FE22
@label=MIN2
g$FE22 DEFW $0000    ; Companion raw outer X-limit word for `FE20`.

; Game status buffer entry at FE24
@label=LIM1
g$FE24 DEFW $0000    ; Current shipped read: primary hill-clipped outer limit pair derived by
                     ; `MHLC` from `FE1C/FE1E/FE20/FE22`.

; Game status buffer entry at FE26
@label=LIM2
g$FE26 DEFW $0000    ; Companion primary hill-clipped outer limit word for `FE24`.

; Game status buffer entry at FE28
@label=LIM3
g$FE28 DEFW $0000    ; Current shipped read: secondary / inner hill-limit pair derived by `SHLC`
                     ; for the interior infill pass.

; Game status buffer entry at FE2A
@label=LIM4
g$FE2A DEFW $0000    ; Companion secondary / inner hill-limit word for `FE28`.

; Game status buffer entry at FE2C
@label=HLCNT
g$FE2C DEFW $0000    ; Notebook name preserved. Current shipped-behaviour read: live hill-data
                     ; stream pointer. Initialised to `$6900` and adjusted by the player
                     ; turn/motion path before `MHLPT` / `SHLPT` consume it via `SP`.

; Game status buffer entry at FE2E
@label=SHCNT
g$FE2E DEFW $0000    ; Notebook name preserved. In shipped code this word behaves as the moving
                     ; inner-row stream pointer used by `SHLPTStepUpRow`.

; Game status buffer entry at FE30
@label=LIM
g$FE30 DEFW $0000    ; Current best shipped read: temporary inner-width / limit pair used by
                     ; `SHLPT` while stepping through the infill region.

; Game status buffer entry at FE32
@label=XLOC
g$FE32 DEFW $0000    ; Notebook name preserved. Current shipped read: pointer to the current X
                     ; source-coordinate list for shared transform/perspective passes. In attract
                     ; mode this is repointed to fixed title/logo X tables.

; Game status buffer entry at FE34
@label=YLOC
g$FE34 DEFW $0000    ; Notebook name preserved. Current shipped read: pointer to the current Y
                     ; source-coordinate list. In the attract title tumble hack this is repointed
                     ; to the first rotated output table so the normal pipeline sees a fake Y axis.

; Game status buffer entry at FE36
@label=ZLOC
g$FE36 DEFW $0000    ; Notebook name preserved. Current shipped read: pointer to the current Z
                     ; source-coordinate list for shared transform/perspective passes.

; Game status buffer entry at FE38
@label=XPERS
g$FE38 DEFW $0000    ; Notebook name preserved. Current shipped read: workspace end-pointer into the
                     ; X perspective output buffer (`XPERS` base around `$DE90`). `PERSP` writes
                     ; downward via `SP`/`PUSH`, so callers often seed this with an interior address
                     ; such as `$DE98` or `$DEC4`.

; Game status buffer entry at FE3A
@label=YPERS
g$FE3A DEFW $0000    ; Companion workspace end-pointer into the Y perspective output buffer
                     ; (`YPERS` base around `$DEC8`), again typically seeded with an interior
                     ; address before the descending `SP`-based write pass.

; Game status buffer entry at FE3C
@label=XMAX
g$FE3C DEFW $0000    ; Notebook name preserved. Current shipped read: visible/projected X upper
                     ; limit tracked by `PERSPTrackVisibleRange` and then reused by caller-side
                     ; visibility / hill-suppression logic.

; Game status buffer entry at FE3E
@label=XMIN
g$FE3E DEFW $0000    ; Companion visible/projected X lower limit tracked by `PERSPTrackVisibleRange`.

; Game status buffer entry at FE40
@label=DYCNT
g$FE40 DEFW $0000    ; Current shipped read: `PERSP` point-count / pass-control slot. Seeded from
                     ; `A` on entry, then reused to control the secondary projection pass.

; Game status buffer entry at FE42
@label=XTAB
g$FE42 DEFW $0000    ; Notebook name preserved. Current shipped read: pointer to the active X-side
                     ; rotation/step table family for `RotateXZLists`. Often seeded from `XTAB`
                     ; (`$D9D0`) or object-specific interior offsets.

; Game status buffer entry at FE44
@label=YTAB
g$FE44 DEFW $0000    ; Notebook name preserved. No confident direct shipped-code role is isolated
                     ; yet; current transform/projection paths appear to use `YLOC`/`FE34` rather
                     ; than this slot directly.

; Game status buffer entry at FE46
@label=ZTAB
g$FE46 DEFW $0000    ; Notebook name preserved. Current shipped read: pointer to the active Z-side
                     ; rotation/step table family for `RotateXZLists`. Often seeded from `ZTAB`
                     ; (`$DAC4`) or object-specific interior offsets.

; Game status buffer entry at FE48
@label=MMAT
g$FE48 DEFW $0000    ; Current shipped read: saved source-word continuation from the first
                     ; `RotateXZLists` pass, preserved between passes and reused by the later
                     ; transform phases as a compact pointer/sign carrier.

; Game status buffer entry at FE4A
@label=XDIS
g$FE4A DEFW $0000    ; Notebook name preserved. Current shipped read: current X displacement /
                     ; world-offset word fed into `RotateXZLists` for the active entity/effect or
                     ; obstacle/object.

; Game status buffer entry at FE4C
@label=ZDIS
g$FE4C DEFW $0000    ; Companion current Z displacement / world-offset word fed into
                     ; `RotateXZLists`.

; Game status buffer entry at FE4E
@label=MUCNT
g$FE4E DEFW $0000    ; Shared small count/control slot. In `RotateXZLists` it is the active element
                     ; count reused by each transform pass; in `PlayStartTheme` it becomes the
                     ; 10-phrase countdown; in the zero-lives branch it becomes the outer
                     ; drip-frame countdown.

; Game status buffer entry at FE50
@label=EXBLP
g$FE50 DEFW $0000    ; Notebook name preserved. Current shipped read: pointer to the last radar /
                     ; status blip byte. `RADARClearWorkspace` clears the previously plotted byte via
                     ; this slot before `RADARPlotBlip` updates it to the new destination.

; Game status buffer entry at FE52
@label=EXSCN
g$FE52 DEFW $0000    ; Notebook name preserved. Current shipped read: persistent radar/proximity
                     ; helper-table base, initialised to `$6300`. `RADARClearWorkspace`
                     ; temporarily uses it via `SP` while clearing transient radar state, and later
                     ; entity logic samples its first byte as a proximity/range reference.

; Game status buffer entry at FE54
@label=TRIGA
g$FE54 DEFW $0000    ; Notebook name preserved, but shipped behaviour is now clear: fire-request
                     ; latch. Keyboard/Kempston decode ORs fire into this slot, and the player-fire
                     ; path at `0x97D6` consumes and clears it.

; Current best decoded movement-state byte:
; `0x00` idle, `0x80` forward, `0x40` back, `0xA0` forward+left, `0x90`
; forward+right, `0x60` back+left, `0x50` back+right, `0x08` left on the
; spot, `0x04` right on the spot.
@label=KMOV
g$FE56 DEFW $0000

; Game status buffer entry at FE58
@label=SIGHT
g$FE58 DEFW $0000    ; Notebook name preserved. Current shipped read: one-frame sight / targeting
                     ; cue latch. Tank, supertank, and missile visibility/setup paths set it to
                     ; `$80`, and the later screen-overlay phase consumes and clears it while
                     ; drawing the extra sight marker.

; Game status buffer entry at FE5A
@label=SP2
g$FE5A DEFW $0000    ; Stack pointer scratch slot 2.

; Game status buffer entry at FE5C
@label=TURN
g$FE5C DEFW $0000

